		{"id":"n-comment","type":"text","text":"THE MAIN MACHINE — every session runs this. start/end are mechanical; boot is a sub-machine; THE FRONT DESK IS HOME. Seeding is a FUNCTION (se_seed_expedition, se_seed_iteration) — no start doors. Above the desk: the ad hoc pair (archive · expeditions). Below: the planned pair. On the right, top to bottom: overhaul, retro — plain states per the ONE-STATE RULE — then ideation, a sub-machine. Overhaul sits directly above retro because they are a pair: the retro moves the standard, the overhaul catches the system up to it. THERE IS NO IDLE STATE (owner ruling 2026-08-23). Idle was a switchboard whose doors the desk already borrowed, so the desk became the switchboard.","x":-380,"y":-1200,"width":700,"height":140},
